@page
@model elite_dangerous_colonise.Pages.AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Page";
    ViewData["Description"] = "This page contains information about ED Colonise.";
    ViewData["url"] = "https://edcolonise.net/About";
    ViewData["Theme"] = "None";
}
@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/lib/flowbite/flowbite.min.js"></script>
    <script>
        $("[data-accordion-target]").on("click", function () {
            const button = $(this);

            $("[data-accordion-target]").each(function () {
                const button = $(this);

                RemoveActiveClasses(button);
            });

            if (button.attr("aria-expanded") === "false") {
                AddActiveClasses(button);
            }
            else {
                RemoveActiveClasses(button);
            }
        });

        function AddActiveClasses(button) {
            const span = button.find("span");
            const svg = button.find("svg");

            button.addClass("!bg-accent text-web-white")
                .removeClass("bg-white text-web-black");
            span.addClass("text-web-white")
                .removeClass("text-web-black");
            svg.addClass("text-web-white")
                .removeClass("text-web-black");
        }

        function RemoveActiveClasses(button) {
            const span = button.find("span");
            const svg = button.find("svg");

            button.addClass("bg-white text-web-black")
                .removeClass("!bg-accent text-web-white");
            span.addClass("text-web-black")
                .removeClass("text-web-white");
            svg.addClass("text-web-black")
                .removeClass("text-web-white");
        }
    </script>
}
<section class="bg-web-white mt-3 mb-3 w-full rounded-md p-3">
    <h1 class="text-web-black p-1 text-center text-xl sm:text-left">About</h1>
    <div data-accordion="collapse" class="mt-3">
        <div id="about-heading-1" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-t-lg border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-1">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">What is ED Colonise?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-1" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-1">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>
                    ED Colonise is a tool designed to make finding colonisation candidates easier.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-2" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-2">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">How do I use ED Colonise?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-2" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-2">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p class="ml-5">
                    Simply clicking "Search" will display all colonisable systems within a specific region, sorted by value. However, these results may be too far away for your liking, lack the required bodies for your desired economy, or already be claimed or locked (but not reported as such).
                    <br /><br />
                    To find results that are more suited to your colonisation goals, you will need to refine your search. To do this, click "More Options" and a range of parameters will appear.
                    <br /><br />
                    Once you've executed a search, a list of system names will be displayed under the search bar. Clicking on one of these names will display a summary of the system's details as well as the names and locations of nearby stations that you can use for colonisation.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Reference System:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    To expand a colony in a specific location, a colonised reference system can be specified. This will refine a search to only show colonisable systems within a specific distance of the reference system. By default, this is set to 15ly but can be increased to 100ly using the "Max Distance From Reference System" slider.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Faction:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    To expand a faction, you can enter its name into the "Faction" box. By default, this will refine a search to only include systems that can be colonised from a <b>station</b> that is controlled by the specific faction. The faction search mode can be toggled to only show systems that can be colonised from a <b>system</b> that is controlled by the faction.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Distance From Region Centre:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    If you don't want to colonise too far from a region's centre, a max distance can be set. This will refine the search to only include results within the specified distance.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Landable and Walkable Bodies:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    To specify how many bodies built on you can specify landable and walkable body counts. This will refine the search to only include systems that have a number of landable and walkable bodies that is within the specified range.
                    <br /><br />
                    <b>Landable Bodies vs Walkable Bodies</b>
                    <br />
                    Landable bodies are bodies that your ship can land on and deploy an SRV on.
                    <br />
                    Walkable bodies are bodies that you can exit your ship on. All walkable bodies are landable bodies, but conditions like extreme gravity can prevent you from exiting your ship. Bodies that are not walkable may not support construction.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Body Counts:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    If you want to get specific about the types of bodies you want in your colony, you can specify how many of each body and colony influencer you would like. Each slider has an icon that displays how it will affect the economy of stations built around that influencer.
                    <br /><br />
                    <b>Economy Influencers vs Economy Boosters</b>
                    <br />
                    Economy influencers increase their specified economy type for a given station built around the influencers. Stations with the "Colony" economy type will be completely replaced by the economy specified by the economy influencers.
                    <br />
                    Economy boosters increase the strength of economy influencers but do not affect the economy by themselves. "Terraformable Bodies" and "Volcanic Bodies" are economy boosters.
                    <br /><br />
                    For a better explanation, read the <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1toXyDQglwVACFKx8umXhP8QcMSAUYPcP6k3STIV2-hE" class="text-blue-800 underline">Colonisation Mega Guide</a>.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Hotspots:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    If you want a specific hotspot type to be present in one of the rings within your colony, you can select a range of hotspot types to refine your search. A long list of hotspots may result in few or no results.
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">Sorting:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    There are a few different sorting options you can select when executing a search: "System Value", "Most Walkable Bodies", "Most Hotspots", "Distance to Region Centre", and "Distance to Reference System".
                </p>
                <h2 class="mt-5 text-lg font-bold">General Notes:</h2>
                <p class="ml-5">
                    This tool is not perfect, and not all colonisable systems in the database are up to date with their current claim status, and some are arbitrarily locked by FDev. As such, <b>you should always check colonisation candidates using the in-game colonisation map mode.</b>
                    <br /><br />
                    Additionally, if you want to contribute to the database's current understanding of the galaxy, you can report uncolonisable systems as "Claimed" (if another player has claimed/colonised the system) or "Locked" (if Frontier has prevented the system's colonisation for whatever reason).
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-4" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-4">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">How is system value calculated?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-4" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-4">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>
                    The value of a system is calculated based on the types and quantities of bodies in the system, the number of walkable bodies, and the number of hotspots.
                    <br /><br />
                    Bodies/body features are categorised into three highly scientific, well thought out, and super cool groups and then weighted according to their group.
                </p>
                <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg border">
                    <table class="w-full table-fixed text-center">
                        <tr class="border-b">
                            <th class="border-r">Interesting (1.0)</th>
                            <th class="border-r">Meh (0.5)</th>
                            <th>Boring (0.2)</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border-r">Black Holes</td>
                            <td class="border-r">Rocky Ice Worlds</td>
                            <td>Other Star Types</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="bg-gray-200">
                            <td class="border-r">Neutron Stars</td>
                            <td class="border-r">Rocky Bodies</td>
                            <td>Gas Giants</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border-r">White Dwarves</td>
                            <td class="border-r">Rings</td>
                            <td>High Metal Content Worlds</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="bg-gray-200">
                            <td class="border-r">Earth-like Worlds</td>
                            <td class="border-r">Volcanic Bodies</td>
                            <td>Metal Rich Bodies</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border-r">Water Worlds</td>
                            <td class="border-r"></td>
                            <td>Icy Bodies</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="bg-gray-200">
                            <td class="border-r">Ammonia Worlds</td>
                            <td class="border-r"></td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border-r">Bodies with Geologicals</td>
                            <td class="border-r"></td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="bg-gray-200">
                            <td class="border-r">Bodies with Organics</td>
                            <td class="border-r"></td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="border-r">Terraformable Bodies</td>
                            <td class="border-r"></td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-5">
                    The number of walkable bodies gets multiplied by a weight of 0.6, and the number of hotspots gets multiplied by a weight of 0.8.
                    <br /><br />
                    The sum of (quantities * weights) produces the system's value.
                    <br /><br />
                    Why these weights? ¯\_(ツ)_/¯
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-6" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-6">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">Why do claimed systems still appear in searches?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-6" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-6">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>
                    There is no 100% accurate way to track which systems have been claimed or colonised because players need to opt into sharing this data using 3rd party apps. As such, results can be outdated.
                    <br /><br />
                    If you want to help improve the dataset, you can do two things:
                </p>
                <ol class="ml-5 list-decimal">
                    <li>Start using a third-party app that allows you to opt into sharing your (anonymised) data with <a href="https://github.com/EDCD/EDDN" class="text-blue-800 underline">EDDN</a>. This will help improve all third-party apps that utilise this data. (<a href="https://edcd.github.io/cmdrs-guide.html" class="text-blue-800 underline">More Details</a>)</li>
                    <li>Report systems using the "Report as Locked" and "Report as Claimed" links under every search result produced by this tool. This removes the reported system from your future search results and contributes to a global blocklist for all users.</li>
                </ol>
                <p class="mt-5 font-bold">You should always check colonisation candidates using the in-game colonisation map mode.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-7" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-7">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">Why is a colonised system missing from the reference search box?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-7" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-7">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>If a colonised system is missing from the search box, there are a few possibilities:</p>
                <ul class="ml-5 list-disc">
                    <li>The system was colonised today, and thus the database has not been updated with the new information yet.</li>
                    <li>The system was never sent to EDDN and thus is unknown to the database.</li>
                    <li>The system is outside of the tool's coverage.</li>
                </ul>
                <br />
                <p>
                    The tool's database is updated with new data daily at 5:00 UTC.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-8" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-8">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">Why are some stations listed as "Unknown"?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-8" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-8">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>
                    Stations are marked as "Unknown" when the database has incomplete data about a colonised system. The tool has correctly identified that the system has been colonised, but detailed information about stations in the system has not been uploaded yet.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div id="about-heading-10" class="grid">
            <button type="button" class="border-web-black text-web-black flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-3 border border-t-1 border-b-1 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm hover:bg-accent-hover rtl:text-right" data-accordion-target="#about-body-10" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="about-body-10">
                <span class="text-web-black flex items-center font-bold">What is the best way to provide feedback or report issues/bugs?</span>
                <svg data-accordion-icon class="h-3 w-3 shrink-0 rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">
                    <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5" />
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div id="about-body-10" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="about-heading-10">
            <div class="border-web-black border border-t-0 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
                <p>
                    Currently, the best way to contact me about ED Colonise is by commenting on the Frontier Forum post for this tool.
                </p>
                <br />
                <a href="https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/introducing-edcolonise-net-a-colonisation-candidate-finder.635882/" target="_blank" class="text-blue-800 underline">Link to the Frontier Forum post.</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>